{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42136 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "Neoclovene is implicated in the biological activity of SNU-387 through a series of molecular targets, all of which are classified as MIPs (molecular interaction proteins). The evidence suggests that Neoclovene interacts with multiple MIPs, each of which is a target of a different compound. Specifically, Neoclovene is shown to interact with (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, which is a complex and highly specific molecule. Similarly, Neoclovene also interacts with Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and another complex compound, both of which are also targets of SNU-387. These findings suggest that Neoclovene may act through a common mechanism by targeting MIPs that are involved in the biological activity of SNU-387. The evidence supports a potential role for Neoclovene in modulating the activity of SNU-387 through interaction with these molecular targets, although the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
